WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.640
- Would you do a like a reboot?

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.163
Like a third, a third time over?

00:00:03.163 --> 00:00:05.220
- A reboot?
- A reboot.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.102
- Yeah, I mean--
- Reboot.

00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:09.219
I love the show!
- Thank you.

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:10.168
We love--
- I love it!

00:00:10.168 --> 00:00:11.010
- Doing it.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.150
We shoot on this lot.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:12.983
- And it's been great.

00:00:12.983 --> 00:00:14.197
I mean, people use to ask me years ago,

00:00:14.197 --> 00:00:15.030
"Would you do it again?"

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.730
But the word reboot didn't exist.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:18.830
It was like, reboots were like--

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:19.663
- [Kelly] It's everywhere now.

00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:20.496
- A Very Brady Christmas.

00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:21.329
Was that, you know what I mean.

00:00:21.329 --> 00:00:23.890
There wasn't like the show done again.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.508
So this has been so great,
and, yes, we'd do it again.

00:00:26.508 --> 00:00:29.440
We'd probably have to
call it The Golden Girls.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.770
But but it's--
(audience laughs)

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.240
- You should do The Golden Boys.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.613
- The Golden--
- You can do the Golden,

00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:35.480
and use your beard.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.340
- Yes, the next, if there's--
- You can be the youngest.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.490
- If there's another reboot, Will is

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.507
definitely getting the beard,
'cause I'm getting too lazy.

00:00:39.507 --> 00:00:41.800
- Oh my God, that is a show for men.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.230
To do Golden Girls, but a (Kelly murmurs).

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.600
I'm just saying, I just came up with it.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:45.433
Use it.
- Sure, sure.

00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:47.284
- I'm, you're welcome.
If I sell that next week

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:50.333
you would sue me.
- One word, one third.

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.480
That's the Nashville way.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.360
I'm just kidding.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:56.470
How did you celebrate
the last show ending?

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:57.940
- Years ago, well so

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:01.480
that's kinda hard to
remember what that was.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.430
But we all wanted to steal stuff.

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.060
I mean that's what you wanna do, you know?

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:08.030
But Max, this is the whole
reason the reboot exists.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.380
Max Mutchnick, who created the show,

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.892
moved the entire set to
his alma mater, in Boston.

00:01:12.892 --> 00:01:14.630
Emerson College, which is where it's

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:17.540
been standing for 10 years,
in tact, everything on it.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.373
- What?

00:01:18.373 --> 00:01:21.350
- And when they finally said,
"Did you take your set back?"

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.750
That's when he said, "I'm
gonna reboot this show."

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.217
And took the flew the
set across the country.

00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.750
But the thing I wanted, there it was,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.570
it showed up again two
years ago on the set.

00:01:29.570 --> 00:01:30.774
I was staring at it.

00:01:30.774 --> 00:01:33.110
And this what happened was, our very

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.240
first interview we ever did in 1998.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.978
Donny and Marie came to visit the set.

00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:38.220
- Wow!
- And Donny had these

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.290
questions on blue cards, and
just as they were rolling,

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:43.450
he shoved them into a box
on Will's coffee table.

00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:45.420
Which remained there, not only for

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.864
our entire eight year run,

00:01:46.864 --> 00:01:49.470
but for the 10 years that
it was at Emerson College.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.411
And the set came back,
we set up over here,

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.660
and I turned to my producer.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:55.120
I said, "If Donny Osmond's questions are

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.080
in that box, I'm taking it."

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.673
And there they were, 20 years later.

00:01:58.673 --> 00:01:59.647
(audience sighs)
Yeah, isn't that funny?

00:01:59.647 --> 00:02:00.480
- What!
(audience applauds)

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.090
That's kind of nuts!

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:04.340
That somebody wouldn't have stolen them!

